From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: drop a redundant enum typedef and receive an ignored HRESULT

Two more -Werror diagnostics in device.cpp, both narrow.

CreateFence declares `typedef enum DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_FLAGS {...}
DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_FLAGS;` at function scope. That is a C idiom: in
C++ the enum-specifier already introduces the type name, so the typedef name
is redundant and nothing uses it, which -Wunused-local-typedefs reports. The
enumerators are used, immediately below, and are untouched -- only the
duplicate name goes.

ReportError calls pfnEscapeCb for a device-status query and deliberately
ignores the result; the comment above it explains why, and that intent is
kept. The existing `(void)` cast does not satisfy GCC's warn_unused_result,
which is only met by actually receiving the value, so the result is stored
and then marked unused. Same shape as the hr fix in 0008.
---
diff --git a/src/device.cpp b/src/device.cpp
index 02c79e8..9b96a7b 100644
--- a/src/device.cpp
+++ b/src/device.cpp
@@ -692,7 +692,12 @@ namespace D3D11On12
             EscapeCB.pPrivateDriverData = &StateCheck;
             EscapeCB.PrivateDriverDataSize = sizeof(StateCheck);
             EscapeCB.Flags.DeviceStatusQuery = 1;
-            (void)m_pKTCallbacks->pfnEscapeCb(nullptr, &EscapeCB);
+            // Best-effort: a failure here only means the device-status
+            // query did not happen. A (void) cast does not satisfy
+            // warn_unused_result, so receive the value and drop it.
+            const HRESULT escapeStatus =
+                    m_pKTCallbacks->pfnEscapeCb(nullptr, &EscapeCB);
+            (void)escapeStatus;
         }
         DeviceBase::ReportError(hr);
     }
@@ -1231,13 +1236,13 @@ namespace D3D11On12
     {
         D3D11on12_DDI_ENTRYPOINT_START();
 
-        typedef enum DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_FLAGS
+        enum DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_FLAGS
         {
             DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_SHARED = 0x1,
             DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_SHARED_CROSS_ADAPTER = 0x2,
             DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_DEFERRED_WAITS = 0x4,
             DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_MONITORED = 0x10
-        } DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_FLAGS;
+        };
 
         D3D12TranslationLayer::FENCE_FLAGS TranslationFlags =
             ((DXGIInternalFenceFlags & DXGI_INTERNAL_CREATEFENCE_DEFERRED_WAITS)       ? D3D12TranslationLayer::FENCE_FLAG_DEFERRED_WAITS       : D3D12TranslationLayer::FENCE_FLAG_NONE) |
